# Caddy config for the wha stack: terminates HTTPS with Caddy's internal CA
# (self-signed, no public domain needed) and reverse-proxies to wha.
#
# WHA_SITE_ADDRESS is the hostname or IP you type into a browser (e.g.
# wha.local or the Pi's LAN IP) — set it in .env or the environment before
# `docker compose up` (scripts/install.sh prompts for it and writes it there).
#
# `tls internal` forces Caddy's local CA even for a bare IP/hostname SAN,
# where a public CA could never issue a certificate. Trust the root it
# generates on each device via the in-UI guide at https://<address>/setup.
{$WHA_SITE_ADDRESS} {
	tls internal
	reverse_proxy wha:8080
}
